From: Orange Pi 3 PCIe reference build
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: orangepi-3: pin vendor PCIe clocks

The vendor H6 Linux 3.10 stack that transfers data reliably through the
on-board mini-PCIe slot programs PCIE_MAXI to 200 MHz and PCIE_AUX to 1 MHz.
The Linux 5.7.4 reference DTS names both clocks but does not assign their
rates, leaving the result dependent on inherited boot state and clock
defaults.

Pin only those two existing H6 CCU clocks on Orange Pi 3.  Do not change the
clock parents, PCIe controller driver, reset or power sequencing, kernel
command line, or guarded r8169 driver.  This makes the first modern-kernel
vendor-stack comparison a DTB-only, two-rate A/B test.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h6-orangepi-3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h6-orangepi-3.dts
@@ -214,6 +214,8 @@
 };
 
 &pcie {
+	assigned-clocks = <&ccu CLK_PCIE_MAXI>, <&ccu CLK_PCIE_AUX>;
+	assigned-clock-rates = <200000000>, <1000000>;
 	vcc-supply = <&reg_bldo2>;
 	vdd-supply = <&reg_dcdcd>;
 	slot-supply = <&reg_vcc33_wifi>;
-- 
